/*Q30. Write a Java program that prompts the user for a character, converts it to its ASCII value, and displays the result.
Input Format:
• The input is the character (alphabet/ digit/ special character).
Output Format:
• The output is the integer that represents the ASCII value.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class AsciiValue {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        char ch = sc.nextLine().charAt(0);
        int ascii = (int) ch;
        System.out.println(ascii);
        sc.close();
    }
}
